g him their  sensitive military data in its memory  when Finn Rey and the other heroes  believe they're sinking to their deaths  and the rise of Skywalker Finn tries to  tell ray something but he never gets the  chance thankfully the hero survived and  when Ray ask Ben what he was going to  tell her he says he'll tell her later  Poe teases Finn about it but by the end  of the film we still haven't learned  whatever it was been meant to say the  most obvious assumption is that he was  going to profess his love for her the  two obviously cared for one another and  shortly after they meet in the force  awakens  Finn asks her pointedly if she has a  boyfriend got a boyfriend a boyfriend  none of your business that's why  according to a cinema blend report  quoting rise of Skywalker director and  co-writer JJ Abrams however Finn's  motivations may have been decidedly less  romantic rather than making a play for  Rey he was apparently going to confirm  something suggested repeatedly  throughout the sequel trilogy named  that he's force-sensitive there are two  big hints in the rise of Skywalker that  pin might have enough of a connection  with the forest to be trained as a Jedi  first there's when finishers fellow  reformed stormtrooper Janna that it was  the force that made it possible for his  true self to emerge from the first  orders conditioning or surprise together  later in the battle against the final  order fleet Finn says he knows the order  has transferred their navigation from  the ground tower to the command ship  only because he could feel it when we  think back to the force awakens there  were hints since the very beginning Finn  makes a memorable impression on kylo Ren  after the village is slaughtered in the  movies opening later when he escapes  with Poe kylo knows which stormtrooper  he was right away the one from the  village affirmed to 187 both moments  suggest Ben is either causing or being  affected by ripples in the force which  kylo feels as well